lt":null,"title":null,"isSectionContent":false,"visibility":{"desktop":true,"mobile":true},"style":{"mobile":{},"desktop":{"width":"245px","height":"106px","background-color":"transparent","position":"absolute","top":"-1px","left":"26px","opacity":null}},"data":{"component":null},"children":[],"pageNames":[],"classList":[],"link":null,"enableEdit":true,"enableDrag":true,"enableDrop":false,"enableResize":{"top":true,"bottom":true,"left":true,"right":true},"selected":false,"useMinHeight":true,"innerHtml":"<button onclick=\"window.history.go(-1); return false;\"\r\nstyle=\"background-color:transparent;border:none;box-shadow:none\">\r\n\r\n<img width=\"178\" height=\"100\" src=\"LOGO%20small.png\" alt=\"logo\">\r\n</button>\r\n<script>\r\nfunction goBack() {\r\n  window.history.back();\r\n}\r\n</script>"},{"id":"silex-id-1604063015245-7","type":"text-element","alt":null,"title":null,"isSectionContent":false,"visibility":{"desktop":true,"mobile":true},"style":{"mobile":{},"desktop":{"width":"957px","height":"768px","position":"absolute","top":"50px","left":"0px"}},"data":{"component":null},"children":[],"pageNames":[],"classList":[],"link":null,"enableEdit":true,"enableDrag":true,"enableDrop":false,"enableResize":{"top":true,"bottom":true,"left":true,"right":true},"selected":false,"useMinHeight":true,"innerHtml":"<p>\n\n</p><p>Digi Card Therapy is an innovative website providing digital tools and content for therapists and coaches from all approaches. The site was built especially for the community of therapists for the challenging period when many of the treatments take place outside the clinic space, and are conducted remotely. In addition, the site is also suitable for anyone interested in self-improvement.</p><p><br></p><p><b>Adam Leighton</b>, one of the founders of the site, is himself a qualified therapist who is trained in various </p><img src=\"https://editor.silex.me/ce/dropbox/get/PROFILE2%20L_180x165(1).png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wysiwyg-float-right\"><p>therapeutic approaches, including highly innovative approaches such as ACT and wilderness adventure nature therapy. After years of a satisfying career, and out of a desire to devote all his time to working with people, Adam made a switch to the field, uniting his love to working with people and nature.</p><p>Adam runs a thriving clinic and invests his life to working with patients and creating create tools for dealing with challenges and creating meaning.</p><p>· &nbsp; Adam is the co-founder and lecturer in the \"Course for the training of CBT-based group facilitators combined with experiential work in nature.\"</p><p></p><p></p><ul><li>Chairman of a charity for Primary Psychological Treatment in England - Heads Up.</li><li>Certified wilderness adventure therapy facilitator.</li><li>Member of the Israeli Association for Low Intensity Cognitive Behavioral Therapy.</li><li>Co-Founder of the Center for Remote Relations with Dr. Arnon Rolnik.</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p><b>We at Digi Card Therapy believe in creating as rich a content world as possible that allows as much flexibility as possible for the therapist's or coaches needs.</b></p><p><br></p><p><b>Mirit Shoham</b>&nbsp;, co-founder, has a bachelor's degree in psychology, and is studying for a master's degree in family studies in an individual counseling program. She treats cognitive-behavioral therapy (low intensity) in adults.</p><p><br></p><p></p>"},{"id":"silex-id-1604132751349-9","type":"text-element","alt":null,"title":null,"isSectionContent":false,"visibility":{"desktop":true,"mobile":true},"style":{"mobile":{},"desktop":{"width":"485px","height":"64px","position":"absolute","top":"7px","left":"-1.000030517578125px"}},"data":{"component":null},"children":[],"pageNames":[],"classList":[],"link":null,"enableEdit":true,"enableDrag":true,"enableDrop":false,"enableResize":{"top":true,"bottom":true,"left":true,"right":true},"selected":false,"useMinHeight":true,"innerHtml":"<h1>About Us</h1>"},{"id":"silex-id-160451441388